From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:55:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 116/119] Bluetooth: btqcomipc: build without the NVMEM BD
 address quirks

HCI_QUIRK_USE_BDADDR_NVMEM and HCI_QUIRK_BDADDR_NVMEM_BE come from a
separate, unmerged series that reads the BD address from an NVMEM cell;
7.2 has neither. Leave the address to userspace, which sets it through
set_bdaddr (qca_set_bdaddr) as the board firmware does: base MAC + 4.
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btqcomipc.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btqcomipc.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btqcomipc.c
index 9d71fe611..9e56d1c8e 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btqcomipc.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btqcomipc.c
@@ -996,10 +996,10 @@ static int btqcomipc_setup(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
-	/* Obtain and set BD address from NVMEM cell */
-	hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_USE_BDADDR_NVMEM);
-	hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_BDADDR_NVMEM_BE);
-
+	/*
+	 * 7.2 has no NVMEM-backed BD address in the HCI core; the board's
+	 * address is set from userspace through set_bdaddr instead.
+	 */
 	return 0;
 }
 
